00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:11.030
like my hair just hates all silicones that's
another misconception silicones aren't all

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:15.250
the same there's a massive variety i found
that my hair loves products with different

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:20.290
silicones like amodimethicone and bisaminopropyl
dimethicone these are silicones that have

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:24.630
a positive charge so they tend to deposit
less on hair positive charges repel each other

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.950
so once there's enough silicone stuck to your
hair then extra stuff doesn't stick on as

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.630
much and so the chance of your hair getting
overloaded with silicones is a lot lower

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:38.540
on top of this the same name on an ingredient
list could mean different substances going

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:43.760
back to dimethicone dimethicone is a silicone
polymer that has oxygen and silicon atoms

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.400
stuck together like this but the polymer can
have different lengths and still be called

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.880
dimethicone and these different lengths will
have different properties if it's longer then

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.810
the dimethicone will feel a bit thicker and
heavier if it's shorter length then it can

00:07:55.810 --> 00:08:00.180
feel more lightweight and spread through hair
a lot more easily if you look at all the different

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.620
ingredients that are called dimethicone that
you can buy you'll see that there are lots

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.900
of different grades and when i say grades
i'm not talking about higher and lower quality

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:11.690
i'm just talking about different dimethicones
with different properties that are good for

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.820
different uses

